- [done, claude] Turn facade into board query object that can be accessed
  through the ConnectIt Function Library
  - Added GetAllGridTiles / GetEmptyGridTiles / IsTileEmpty /
    GetGridTilesWithFactionPieces / GetTileAtPosition /
    GetRandomEmptyGridTile / IsGameBoardFull / HasFactionWon to
    UConnectIt_GameUtilityLibrary, reading from the replicated board
    state (UConnectIt_BoardStateComponent) instead of the old
    UConnectIt_GameFacade (which reads from the non-networked
    UConnectIt_State_Game / UGameTurnParticipant stack).
  - Left UConnectIt_GameFacade/ViewModel/State_* in place -- they may
    still back the old _ConnectIt (non-networked) content. Revisit once
    it's confirmed nothing in _ConnectIt still needs them.
- [done, claude] make abstract grid cursor manager
  - Added AGridCursorManagerBase (UnrealGridMechanics/Cursor) -- abstract
    actor owning the hover subscription (UGridWorldSubsystem::
    OnGridTileHoverChanged, the same pipeline UTurnBasedAction hover
    validation uses) and Enable/PauseCursor state. Subclasses only
    implement UpdateCursor(Tile) for the visual.
  - Refactored AGridCursorSimpleBase to derive from it -- now just the
    mesh-follow visual, nothing else.
  - Found + fixed along the way: AGridCursorSimpleBase was previously
    listening to UGridTrackerSubsystem::OnGridTileHoveredStart, which
    never fires -- AGridTileBase::BeginPlay only registers with the
    newer UGridWorldSubsystem (registration with GridTrackerSubsystem is
    commented out). The cursor was dead code; it now works via the
    subsystem tiles actually register with.
  - Also fixed an inverted bool in the old EnableCursor/PauseCursor pair
    (EnableCursor(true) was calling PauseCursor(true), which disabled
    updates while unhiding the actor).
  - Not wired into any Blueprint yet -- no asset currently references
    GridCursorSimpleBase, so this needs a BP_ or placement in a level to
    actually be used.

- [done, claude] Fix ConnectIt_PlacePieceAction -- IsValidHoverTile_Implementation
  and HandleValidSelection_Implementation were stubbed out (hardcoded
  return false / empty body), referencing a nonexistent
  AGridTileBase::GetGridPosition(). No tile could ever be hovered or
  placed. Restored using UConnectIt_GameUtilityLibrary::GetGridPositionForTile
  to resolve position via the tile registry instead. Not verified against
  a real engine build (no local UE install in this environment) -- build
  and playtest in editor before trusting it.
